# Luminary marker — 1.9.21 release + cli#479
- date: 2026-11-07
- branch: release-1.9.21
- lead: michael-feathers
- supporting: [tony-hoare]

## What each lens caught

- michael-feathers (lead) — an injected default is still production code.
  runBuild takes a runner argument, and all three of its tests pass a stub, so
  the default arrow function never ran under test. The seam built for
  testability is exactly what hid the defect inside its own default. The cure
  is a test that exercises the default path, which is now Test 4.
- tony-hoare — postcondition. runBuild's contract is "dist matches
  package.json after this returns". It threw instead of returning, so the
  postcondition was unreachable and the caller reported a failure that had not
  happened. Verified by hand after the fix: dist/cli.js --version reports
  1.9.21, matching package.json.
